---
layout: app-layout.njk
title: Onsight / Redpoint Gap – Climbing Logbook
discipline: true
bundle: performance-gap
staticShellNote: |-
  Genuinely static shell (#348), same pattern as public/map/index.html
         -- see that file's own comment for why every path below is absolute
         and client/performance-gap-main.js reads the username from
         location.pathname itself rather than this file being templated.
---
<div class="max-w-[960px] mx-auto">
  <!-- Picker/menu row before the brand row, and align-left on
       <climbing-header> -- matches /logbook's own layout (left-aligned
       brand row below the header row, not centered above it). Found via
       Raven's production report, 2026-08-10 -- see climbing-header.js's
       own comment on the align-left attribute. -->
  <climbing-page-header></climbing-page-header>

  <div class="flex items-end gap-3 mb-5" id="picker-tabs-row">
    <climbing-discipline-picker></climbing-discipline-picker>
    <climbing-tab-bar active-page="performance"></climbing-tab-bar>
  </div>

  <!-- #601 -- same btn back-link pattern as public/account/edit/
       index.html's own back-to-account-link; href set client-side in
       client/performance-gap-main.js once USERNAME is known. -->
  <a class="btn btn-primary mt-4 mb-5" id="back-to-performance-link" href="#">
    <svg class="w-[.9rem] h-[.9rem] stroke-current fill-none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m15 18-6-6 6-6"></path></svg>
    Performance Insights
  </a>

  <!-- #620 -- report-style prose, not a bordered/background card --
       same <climbing-grade-pyramid>'s own #window-note pattern (flowing
       paragraphs, inline <strong> emphasis, no box). The mirror image of
       #597's own per-field entry-form captions: this names which field
       feeds this view. -->
  <div class="mb-5" id="view-explainer">
    <p class="text-[.95rem] text-foreground leading-[1.7]">How your first-attempt sends compare to your eventual sends over time — is the gap between the two closing, or is one metric stalling?</p>
    <p class="text-[.82rem] text-muted leading-[1.7] mt-2">Two lines track your best first-attempt (flash/onsight) grade and your best eventual-send grade per period; the bars behind them show average <strong class="text-foreground font-semibold">attempts</strong> needed per send. Built from the <strong class="text-foreground font-semibold">Attempts</strong> count and <strong class="text-foreground font-semibold">Flash</strong> selection on each send.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- #111 -- Performance insights are online-only, deliberately, not a
       client-side fallback computed from possibly-stale cached entries
       (Raven's own call: at the crag with poor/no connection, the
       priority is reading/updating the logbook, not reviewing aggregate
       stats -- a "review later" activity). Shown instead of the
       onsight/redpoint gap view when the initial fetch fails; starts
       hidden, toggled in performance-gap-main.js's own boot(). -->
  <div class="row-card text-center max-w-[420px] mx-auto" id="performance-offline" hidden>
    <p class="text-[.9rem] text-foreground">Performance insights need a connection.</p>
    <p class="text-[.82rem] text-muted mt-2">Reconnect and reload this page to see your onsight/redpoint gap.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-3 mb-4">
    <div id="time-window-root"></div>
    <!-- #704 -- which of this discipline's scales the chart below
         renders grades in; client/report-grade-scale-picker.js. -->
    <div id="report-grade-scale-root"></div>
  </div>
  <div id="gap-root"></div><div id="evidence-overlay-root"></div>

  <div class="text-center text-muted text-[.78rem] mt-8" id="footer"></div>
</div>
